    "临床上说“电轴偏转”通常指 QRS 额面电轴，正常约 −30° 至 +90°；P 波电轴也可测量（正常约 0° 至 +75°，异常提示异位房律等），T 波电轴通常与 QRS 主向量大致一致，缺血、电解质紊乱、肥厚\/劳损时可改变。本页三个环可分别调节，仅用于理解向量方向与投影，不把 P\/T 偏转直接等同于 QRS 电轴诊断。": "Clinically, “axis deviation” usually refers to the frontal QRS axis, normally about −30° to +90°; the P-wave axis can also be measured (normally about 0° to +75°; abnormalities suggest ectopic atrial rhythm, etc.), and the T-wave axis usually roughly aligns with the main QRS vector, but may change with ischemia, electrolyte disturbances, or hypertrophy\/strain. The three loops on this page can be adjusted separately; they are only for understanding vector direction and projection, and P\/T deviation is not directly equated with a QRS axis diagnosis.",
